    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0545" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.113 Senate Investigation/75: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-09-25T18:00:00-05:00">September 25,
                            1934—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 26—8 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. With reference to my despatch 335, September 12th,<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d362-f1"/> Colombian Minister for Foreign Affairs<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d362-f2"/> informs me his Government would greatly appreciate it if
                    the two letters from Commander Strong to <pb facs="0546" n="446" xml:id="pg446"
                    /> the Colombian Consul General in New York disclosing certain defense plans of
                    Colombia should be eliminated from the published report of the Senate Munitions
                    Investigating Committee. As the Senate investigations have otherwise been
                    received most favorably in Colombia it is believed that the suppression of the
                    two letters would have a very desirable effect upon the Colombian
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
